    "instructions": "Take the chops out of the fridge 15 minutes early, pat them dry, snip the fat edge in a couple of spots so they sit flat, and season both sides with salt and pepper.\nCore the apples and cut them into thick wedges, skin on. Slice the onion into thin half-moons.\nHeat the oil in a large frying pan over medium-high heat and cook the chops for 3 to 4 minutes a side until golden and just cooked through. Move them to a plate to rest.\nTurn the heat down to medium, add the butter, then the onion, and cook for about 5 minutes until soft and starting to colour.\nAdd the apple wedges and cook, turning now and then, for 5 to 6 minutes until tender and caramelised at the edges but still holding their shape.\nSplash in a few tablespoons of water and scrape up the browned bits, then return the chops and any resting juices to the pan and warm through for a minute. Season to taste and serve with the apples and onion spooned over."
